.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KSPAWN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kspawn
.Nd make a named group of virtual machines from a klab golden, and take it away again
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm spawn
.Fl -name Ar cluster
.Fl -distro Ar distro
.Op Fl -count Ar n
.Op Fl -cpu Ar n
.Op Fl -ram Ar mb
.Op Fl -disk Ar gb
.Op Fl -role Ar role
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm status | destroy
.Ar cluster
.Nm
.Cm ssh
.Ar cluster
.Op Ar n
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes
.Ar n
virtual machines at once, each a ZFS clone of one of klab's goldens,
.Ar pool Ns Pa /vms/klab-golden- Ns Ar distro Ns Pa @golden ,
so they take no time to copy and no space until they change.
Each is named
.Ql kspawn- Ns Ar cluster Ns - Ns Ar NN ,
gets a cloud-init seed that sets its host name and lets root in with this
machine's key, and is started on libvirt's
.Ql default
network.
The machines of a cluster are made in parallel.
.Pp
What was made is recorded in
.Pa /var/lib/kspawn/clusters/ Ns Ar cluster Ns Pa /manifest.json ,
which the other commands read, and in kldload's state database, so the
Ansible inventory
.Xr kldload-inventory 8
sees the nodes at once.
Each node that got an address is then put on the WireGuard mesh with
.Xr kldload-enroll 8 .
.Pp
A cluster name is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, at most 31
characters.
Every command but
.Fl -help
re-runs itself with
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm spawn
Make the cluster.
A node that could not be made is removed \(em its clone and its seed \(em
and its error printed, and the command exits 1.
A node that is made but has no address after three minutes is kept, and
shown without one.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -name Ar cluster
Required; must not exist yet.
.It Fl -distro Ar distro
Required; one whose golden exists:
.Ql centos ,
.Ql rocky ,
.Ql fedora ,
.Ql debian
or
.Ql ubuntu .
.It Fl -count Ar n
Nodes; default 3.
.It Fl -cpu Ar n
Virtual CPUs each; default 2.
.It Fl -ram Ar mb
Memory each, in MB; default 2048.
.It Fl -disk Ar gb
Grow each node's disk to this many GB; the default, 0, keeps the golden's.
It is never shrunk.
.It Fl -role Ar role
The role recorded, and given to the inventory; default
.Ql worker .
.El
.It Cm list
Every cluster, its distribution, node count and when it was made.
.It Cm status Ar cluster
The manifest, then each node's state and address as libvirt sees them now.
.It Cm ssh Ar cluster Op Ar n
Log in to node
.Ar n
(default 1) as root.
.It Cm destroy Ar cluster
Remove every node with
.Ql kvm-delete Ar node Fl -force
\(em the machine, its clone, its seed, its row in the state database and
its mesh peer \(em and then the cluster's record.
With a
.Ev POOL
other than
.Ql rpool ,
which
.Xr kvm-delete 8
does not know,
.Nm
removes the machine, clone, seed and row itself, and not the mesh peer.
Only what
.Cm spawn
would have made for that cluster is touched, whatever the manifest says;
anything else is reported and left.
If a step fails the record is kept, so
.Cm destroy
can be run again.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev POOL
The pool holding the goldens and the clones; default
.Ql rpool .
.It Ev NETWORK
The libvirt network; default
.Ql default .
.It Ev SSH_KEY
The key put in the nodes and used by
.Cm ssh ;
default
.Pa /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 ,
made if missing.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kspawn/clusters/ Ns Ar cluster Ns Pa /manifest.json
The record of a cluster.
.It Pa /var/lib/libvirt/isos/kspawn- Ns Ar cluster Ns - Ns Ar NN Ns Pa -seed.iso
A node's cloud-init seed.
.It Ar pool Ns Pa /vms/kspawn- Ns Ar cluster Ns - Ns Ar NN
A node's disk.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done; for
.Cm spawn ,
every node came up.
.It 1
A node or a step failed, or a name or number was refused.
.It 2
An unknown command.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, with a throwaway cluster
.Ql kst ,
removed afterwards.
.Xr kldload-enroll 8
was replaced for the test by one that declines, so no mesh peer was left
behind.
