.Ss Taking it away
A second cluster of two nodes, made the same way:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kspawn destroy kst
[kspawn] Destroying cluster 'kst'...
[kspawn]   kvm-delete kspawn-kst-01 --force
Force-stopping VM (running)...
Removing VM definition...
Destroying ZFS zvol: rpool/vms/kspawn-kst-01

Deleted 'kspawn-kst-01'
[kspawn]   kvm-delete kspawn-kst-02 --force
Force-stopping VM (running)...
Removing VM definition...
Destroying ZFS zvol: rpool/vms/kspawn-kst-02

Deleted 'kspawn-kst-02'
[kspawn] Cluster 'kst' destroyed.
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss A node that fails
Before the fix to the seed's bus, on the same machine:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kspawn spawn --name kst --distro debian --count 1 --ram 1024
\&...
[kspawn]   node-1 failed:
      [kspawn]   [kspawn-kst-01] cloning from rpool/vms/klab-golden-debian@golden...
      [kspawn]   [kspawn-kst-01] virt-install (2 CPU, 1024MB, debian12)...
      ERROR    unsupported configuration: IDE controllers are unsupported for this QEMU binary or machine type
\&...
      [kspawn]   [kspawn-kst-01] virt-install failed (its message is above); removing its clone and seed
.Ed
.Ss What it refuses
In a Fedora 44 container.
The last manifest was written by hand to name things
.Nm
did not make:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kspawn destroy ../..
[kspawn] FATAL: cluster name must be lowercase letters, digits and dashes, 1-31 long: '../..'
# (exited 1)
# kspawn spawn --name web --distro debian --count three
[kspawn] FATAL: --count needs a whole number, got 'three'
# (exited 1)
# kspawn destroy empty
[kspawn] FATAL: no manifest in /var/lib/kspawn/clusters/empty; nothing is destroyed without one (remove the directory by hand)
# (exited 1)
# kspawn destroy evil
[kspawn] Destroying cluster 'evil'...
[kspawn]   manifest names 'important-vm', which is not a node of evil; left alone
[kspawn]   manifest names zvol 'rpool/data', which is not one spawn makes; left alone
[kspawn] 2 step(s) failed; the manifest is kept at /var/lib/kspawn/clusters/evil so destroy can be run again
# (exited 1)
.Ed
