.Sh HISTORY
It was written as the first of several runtimes; only KVM was ever
built, and
.Fl -runtime
accepts only
.Ql kvm .
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page, it was found that no cluster could ever
have been made: a clone that
worked was taken for one that failed, the seed needed a program Fedora
does not ship and was attached to a controller the machine does not
have, and
.Cm ssh
used the node's name as its address.
.Cm destroy
left each node's mesh peer on the host; it uses
.Xr kvm-delete 8
since.
In a container,
.Ql kspawn destroy ../../libvirt
removed
.Pa /var/lib/libvirt ,
said the cluster was destroyed, and exited 0; names are checked since.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Root on every node accepts this machine's key, and
.Cm ssh
does not check the node's host key.
.Pp
The goldens are klab's; without
.Ql klab golden Ar distro
there is nothing to clone.
